# Cloudflare / local secrets
.dev.vars*
.env*
.wrangler/
# Node
node_modules/
# OS
.DS_Store

# Scratch probes. Rendering checks and viewport measurements get written into
# tests/ so they can resolve playwright from tests/node_modules, and `git add -A`
# has swept them into a PUBLIC repository three times now. They carry absolute
# paths and no assertions; anything worth keeping becomes a real contract test.
#
# ENUMERATING NAMES IS A LOSING GAME, and the list below is the evidence: it
# caught probe-* and cardshot-* and missed _d2.mjs, which shipped in #18, and
# __chip_probe.html, which was one `--amend` from shipping here. What every one
# of them actually shares is a leading underscore, so that is what is ignored —
# a convention a future probe will follow without this file being updated.
#
# articles/_template/ is the one real leading-underscore path in the tree.
_*
!articles/_template/
!articles/_template/**
tests/*_tmp.mjs
tests/.tmp-*
tests/probe-*.mjs
tests/cardshot-*.mjs

# Emitted-payload scratch directories. Several suites run the pipeline's own
# emitter into tests/ and clean up in a `finally` — which does not run when a
# suite is killed mid-assertion, and leaves a directory of JSON that `git add
# -A` then offers to commit. The dot prefix is the convention those suites
# already use; ignoring the shape rather than the names is the same argument
# the underscore rule above makes.
tests/.*-emit/
tests/.*-probe/

# Screenshot output directories. The design shots are megabytes of PNG that
# regenerate from `_shots-ab.mjs` in two minutes, and every one of them is a
# picture of a state the payloads already describe — so committing them stores
# a stale copy of something reproducible. The precedent is the Phase-0
# candidate sets: shot into a throwaway dir, shared out-of-band, never tracked.
tests/.shots-*/
